# Trivy CVE ignore list — release container scan.
#
# Each entry must include the date added, the upstream source of the
# vulnerable package, and the condition under which it can be removed.
# Re-evaluate before each release: rebuild the image, rescan, and drop
# entries whose Fixed Version is now present in the base image.

# CVE-2026-0861 — glibc memalign integer overflow → heap corruption.
# Package: libc6 (Debian) — supplied by gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian12.
# Status: fix exists in Debian (libc6 2.36-9+deb12u14) but the distroless
# base image had not been rebuilt at the time of the v0.7.12 release, so
# both gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian12:latest and our built image still ship
# 2.36-9+deb12u13. Tracked upstream:
#   https://github.com/GoogleContainerTools/distroless
#
# Remove this line once `trivy image gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian12:latest`
# no longer reports CVE-2026-0861.
# Added: 2026-05-17
CVE-2026-0861
